<blockquote>
<p>The story is about discovery and how much information can actually be obtained with the obstacle of the LLUN aura.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>what is the LLUN aura?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After trying and failing to save Jack from Twist, the SCP agents will be surprised to see that Devillian</p>
</blockquote>
<p>not a critique per se but a comment: it'd be a lot less confusing if you were consistent with how you refer to James Devillian Twist here; sometimes calling him Twist and sometimes Devillian makes it seem like he's two people.</p>
<hr />
<p>I don't hate this conceptually, or the idea of like, Twist as this weird extra-reality assassin endlessly hunting down Jack; but my concern is that there's not a lot of context for <em>why</em>: it feels almost like set dressing here because I don't really know who Jack is, or why Twist wants to kill him and so I don't really have feelings on this because I don't know if this is like &quot;Twist is a ruthless murderer who cannot be stopped&quot; or &quot;Twist is the good guy who will stop at nothing to prevent Jack destroying the world&quot;.</p>
<p>I'm also extremely conflicted because a lot of this plot feels like it'd work best as a tale centred around one of them repeating the mission over and over again, especially since the Foundation involvement here seems to be uh completely minimal? They appear at some point, do some interviews/experiments with uncertain purpose and outcome and then the story ends, and it feels&#8230;underwhelming. Especially when compared to like, the possibility of doing this intense action thing about Twist hunting Jack.</p>
</div>
